My first illiterate ascension.

I apologise for not having much to say about this one at all due to the
timeframe of the game itself.  This one started before last year's
devnull tourneyment and was around the castle or so when I spent
november playing the tourney.  I played this game again a few months
later on and recently felt like finishing it all up. 

Illiterate is quite fun but I had a rough time trying to poly some
scrolls of scare monster for emergencies.  Once I finally got one it got
blessed and fortunately never had to be used.  Terrible luck with armor
wishes.  Everything wished for ended up +0.  Oh well.  Good thing I'm a
valk with that orb of weight. 

In a bonehead move just trying to hurry and finish the game I had
realized (after I got the book from Rodney) that I had not attached
candles and did not have the candles on me either.  Oops.  Good thing
the WoW wasn't empty of that would have really ruined my day.  7 candles
coming right up! 

The force going up was slightly more annoying than usual, but I beat it
eventually.  Not finding a ring of lev or conflict was a bit of a pain,
and I likely should have gone way back up in the dungeon and tried using
the last few charges on a different poly wand I found on them.  But I
figured the ascension would feel better without cheating on astral with
conflict. 

I wasn't even wearing my "oLS.  I guess I never switched to it once I
found out which one it was from Vlad.  That's ok...I don't like getting
killed in my ascensions. 

